Releases are frozen until the v0.3.0 chain is complete.

The UI now talks only to the unified mail delegate. The walk that moves the
identities, contacts and local state of the v0.2.x delegates into it is in
the tree, but the chain is not finished: the scrub of what the walk leaves
behind, the background jobs, inbox v2 and the rehearsal against real v0.2.x
data are still to land, and a release before them would ship a migration
nobody has rehearsed. scripts/check-release-freeze.sh refuses
while this file exists; scripts/release.sh and the publish-email,
publish-container and publish-production tasks run it first. The v0.3.0
release removes it.
